$A_1=1$. Valid bottoms: 2, 3, 6.
If we pair (1, 2), remaining: 3, 6. Can we pair (3, 6)? $3 \le 6/2 = 3$. Yes. Total 2 pairs.
If we pair (1, 6), remaining: 2, 3. Can we pair (2, 3)? $2 \le 3/2 = 1.5$. No. Total 1 pair.
So pairing with the smallest valid bottom seems better here.

